Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.25,0:00:04.30,Guide,,0,0,0,,Imagine a European enterprise software company
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.30,0:00:07.80,Guide,,0,0,0,,expanding into the Middle East.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.20,0:00:10.70,Guide,,0,0,0,,The platform has two main applications:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.70,0:00:11.80,Guide,,0,0,0,,Invoicing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.70,0:00:14.80,Guide,,0,0,0,,and Procurement.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.20,0:00:21.20,Guide,,0,0,0,,The first business requirement sounded simple:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.60,0:00:26.20,Guide,,0,0,0,,support Arabic in both applications.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.20,0:00:33.50,Guide,,0,0,0,,So we switched the language and document direction
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.50,0:00:37.60,Guide,,0,0,0,,from LTR to RTL.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.20,0:00:40.00,Guide,,0,0,0,,But suddenly,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:43.70,Guide,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(1150,130)}several parts of the UI started breaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.20,0:00:48.00,Guide,,0,0,0,,So why did changing the language and direction
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.00,0:00:49.80,Guide,,0,0,0,,break the UI?
